# Finite upper bounds and separating witnesses

Each nontrivial pair spans a three-element line in the binary four-space.
The XOR formula makes the displacement product independent of the ordering
of these three elements, so the same checked rank bound covers the line.

Generated by source/generate.py. The literal ATLAS max1 kernel matrices
and bit convention come from KernelCount.Tables and Janko4.Model.Data.
All numerical witnesses are checked by Lean; Python is not trusted.
-/

